SUMMARY:Sit and Sound Sanctuary
DESCRIPTION:Inner Peace Collective\nDetails: Guided Meditation and Sound B
 ath\n\\*\\*\\* Free Offering to the Community - Monthly Event on the 3rd W
 ednesday (sometimes on the 4th).\n\\*\\*\\* No Experience Required\n\n“S
 it and Sound Sanctuary”\nA monthly gathering for community\, guided medi
 tation\, self-care\, and sound healing.\n\nJoin our us for a chance to com
 e together and connect\, explore our inner realms\, and find some time to 
 cultivate inner peace and a quiet presence.\n\nOur intention is to help ea
 ch other cultivate greater awareness\, and more resilience in body\, mind\
 , and life.\n\nDuring our time together\, we will explore the ancient art 
 of sound healing with Himalayan singing bowls (Vivek) paired with a guided
  meditation facilitated by Dr. Omri Sitton\, D.C.\n\n\\*\\*It’s highly r
 ecommended to arrive at class well-hydrated and with a comfortably satisfi
 ed belly. Aim for a state where you're neither hungry nor overly full—ju
 st nicely in between. This balance will help you achieve the best results 
 during your meditation.\n\n\\*\\* Bring: Cushion or yoga mat if you would 
 like\, chairs will be provided\n\n\\*\\* Please walk around the left side 
 of the library to the last door if you arrive past 6pm.\n\\*\\*Front door 
 will be locked precisely at 6pm.\n\n\\*\\* Guided by Dr. Omri Sitton\, D.C
 .\n\\*\\* Sound Healing Facilitation by Vivek Chugh\n\nDetails:\nWhen: Wed
 nesday\, April 22nd\nWhere: North Asheville Public Library on Merrimon\n10
 30 Merrimon Ave\, Asheville\, NC 28804\nTime: 6:00-7:00pm\n\nHow to find u
 s:\nPlease arrive early to settle in. In case you arrive at 6pm or later\,
  walk around the left side of the library to the last door on the right.\n
 \nFeel Well\, Heal Well\, Live Well.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/inner-peace-collective/events/3136410
 36/
